course: dictionary
lesson: 2596
title: Department
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A department is one part of a big organisation that does one kind of work. A school has a science department and a maths department. «The emergency department was busy all night.» Here, a department is one section of a hospital, the part that deals with sudden, serious illness and injuries.
explain: A department can also be a shop. A department store is a large shop with many sections, each selling a different kind of thing, such as toys, clothes or kitchenware. The words around department tell you which meaning fits, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Words can change from place to place. In the USA and Canada, the «fire department» is called the fire brigade or fire service in the UK, Ireland and Australia. In the USA, a hospital's emergency department is called the ER; in the UK it is called A&E. The job is the same, but the name is different.
fact: A department is one part of a big organisation, such as a school, company, shop or government.
fact: A department store is a large shop with different sections selling many kinds of things.
fact: «The science department» means the teachers and rooms that teach science in a school.
fact: In the USA and Canada, the «fire department» does the job the fire brigade does in the UK.
fact: A&E means Accident and Emergency, the hospital department for sudden, serious illness and injuries; in the USA it is called the ER.
exercise: «The science department» is part of a school. What is a department? | *A part of a big organisation that deals with one kind of work | A kind of hat worn by teachers | A small, quiet room for reading
exercise: What is a department store? | *A large shop with different sections selling many kinds of things | A shop that only sells shoes | A store that sells only food from the sea
exercise: In the USA and Canada, a «fire department» is what? | *A service that puts out fires and helps in emergencies | A shop that sells fire engines | A hot drink served in winter
test: «In the emergency department the most serious cases are seen first.» What does emergency department mean? | A part of a hospital for sudden, serious illness and injuries | A shop that sells emergency supplies | *A part of a hospital for sudden, serious illness and injuries, where the most urgent cases come first
test: «A department store has toys on one floor and clothes on another.» What does department mean in this sentence? | A school for young children | *A section of a shop that sells one kind of thing | A kind of ticket
exam: «In the emergency department the most serious cases are seen first; it is not first come, first served.» What does this tell you? | *The sickest patients may be seen before people who arrived earlier | Everyone waits in the order they arrive | Small cuts are always treated first | The emergency department is closed at night
